course: dictionary
lesson: 15791
title: Unaffected: not changed, and natural
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unaffected is made of two parts. The start, un-, means not, and affected means changed or touched by something. So unaffected means not changed or harmed by something. «The village was unaffected by the flood, because it sat high on the hill.» The water did not reach the village, so it stayed safe.
explain: The word has a second meaning, about people. «She was unaffected when she won the prize, and she just said thank you.» She did not show off or pretend. She was natural and sincere.
explain: Use the swap check: put «not changed by» in place of unaffected and see if the sentence still makes sense. In science, news and maths, unaffected usually means not changed. In stories about people, it usually means natural and sincere.
fact: Unaffected means not changed or harmed by something.
fact: «Unaffected» can also mean natural and sincere, not pretending or showing off.
fact: Useful phrases are «unaffected by» and «remain unaffected».
fact: «The result was unaffected by the temperature.» Scientists check that the heat did not change the answer.
fact: «Un-» at the start of a word often means not, so you can use that clue to work out meanings.
exercise: «The town stayed unaffected by the storm.» What does unaffected mean here? | *Not changed or harmed by the storm | Lost somewhere in the storm | Very wet and cold after the storm
exercise: «He was unaffected by his fame and still shared his lunch with his friends.» What does unaffected suggest? | Hungry and tired | Famous and proud | *Natural and sincere, not showing off | Angry and rude
exercise: «The result remained unaffected by the heat.» Find and copy the word that means not changed. | result | heat | remained | *unaffected
test: «A total is unaffected if you change the order of the numbers.» What does this tell you? | The total is always zero | *The total stays the same | The total gets bigger every time | The numbers disappear
test: Which person is unaffected in the sense of natural and sincere? | The man who shouted at the referee | The boy who showed off his new watch all day | The woman who hid her face from the camera | *The girl who chatted to everyone the same way, with no pretending
exam: Which sentence uses unaffected to mean not changed or harmed? | «She was unaffected, and she thanked everyone warmly.» | «He pretended to be unaffected by the joke, but he laughed.» | *«The house was unaffected by the storm, and nothing broke.»
